From d128e76cc8358628f407c4bdc39339f221e76cfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 07:33:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 96/96] blitz-dom, blitz-paint: lay a table's captions out
 above and below its grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A table-caption child of a table was passed over: neither laid out nor
drawn. CSS 2.2 §17.4 puts a table's captions above its grid (caption-side:
top) or below it, in the table wrapper box, each as wide as the table.

The table context now collects its captions and makes them layout children
of the table, outside the grid. After the grid, layout_captions lays each
out at the table's border-box width less its margins and stacks them above
and below; the cells and the grid's row positions move down by the height
above, and the table's size and baselines grow by it. A height given to the
table is its box's, so the grid gets what the captions leave. Paint draws
the table's own background and border around the grid alone.
---
